{{define "handoff_close" -}}
Run `endless worktree check` and relay anything it prints — it stays silent when the worktree is clean, so a clean handoff says nothing about git. Flag external state (CI, services) only if it's actually in play. Do NOT recap task status, phase, or relationships, and do NOT confirm the negative ("no stray files", "nothing to report").{{if .bg}} You're a background agent — just stop when done; the user reads this with `claude attach`.{{end}}
{{- end}}

{{define "handoff_verify" -}}
Hand me exactly ONE command to verify this — `esu && ./tests/tasks/e-{{.spawned_id}}-verify.sh` — folding this task's own tests into that one suite as a fail-fast check. Do NOT enumerate a manual checklist. Run the project-wide regression (tests, lint, build) yourself and state the result in one line — never as commands for me to run. See `endless guide orchestration`.
{{- end}}

{{define "handoff_nonverify" -}}
This task delivers information, not testable behavior — there is nothing to verify. Do NOT invent a how-to-test, verification steps, or a checklist; point me to the deliverable and stop.
{{- end}}
